0033: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0034:     """
0035:     Draw the missing diagonal connector segment between each pair of same-color rectangular objects.
0036: 
0037:     Input structure:
0038:     - The grid has one dominant background color.
0039:     - Every foreground color appears as exactly two separated solid rectangular 4-connected objects.
0040:     - The two rectangles of each color are diagonally offset with facing corners on a 45-degree line.
0041: 
0042:     Rule:
0043:     - Keep all existing rectangles unchanged.
0044:     - For each foreground color, connect the lower facing corner of the upper rectangle to the upper facing corner of the lower rectangle.
0045:     - Paint only the intervening background pixels on that diagonal, excluding the two endpoint pixels already in the rectangles.
0046: 
0047:     Key insight:
0048:     - Same-color rectangles define the endpoints; the output completes the open diagonal between their nearest facing corners.
0049:     """
