0027:     - Each sprite instance is a scaled copy of one of the two prototypes, placed on the grid.
0028: 
0029:     Rule:
0030:     - Identify the two prototype patterns from the smallest-area sprites.
0031:     - For each sprite, determine which prototype it matches and its integer scale factor.
0032:     - Replace it with the other prototype at the same scale, aligned by an internal anchor region (color-1 pixels).
0033: 
0034:     Key insight: Every sprite toggles to the alternate prototype; the anchor sub-region inside each sprite pins the alignment so swapped sprites land in the correct position regardless of scale.
